<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Newfoundland</h1><p class="st-meta">1610 CE – 1907 CE (approx.) · capital St. John's</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">England's oldest overseas colony in origin, a fishing outpost of the North Atlantic that chose to stay outside Canada for more than 80 years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-cabot">John Cabot</a> reached the region in 1497, and fishing fleets from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, Portugal and the Basque country worked its banks for a century before settlement. In 1610 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-guy">John Guy</a> founded a colony at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cupids">Cupids</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland-company">London and Bristol Company</a>, and other proprietary ventures followed, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-calvert-1st-baron-baltimore">George Calvert</a>'s Avalon at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferryland">Ferryland</a> in 1621.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>For two centuries the migratory cod fishery from the West Country dominated, and fishing admirals and visiting naval officers kept order, while the French held <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/plaisance">Plaisance</a> until 1713. Settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Ireland gradually stayed year-round in outports along the coast, salting cod for markets in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dominion-of-newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> became a formal crown colony in 1825, gained representative government in 1832 and responsible government in 1855 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-francis-little">Philip Francis Little</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Newfoundlanders rejected joining the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canada">Dominion of Canada</a> in the 1869 election. The long dispute over French fishing rights on the French Shore was settled in 1904, and in 1907 the colony became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dominion-of-newfoundland">Dominion of Newfoundland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-newfoundland.jpg" alt="Colony of Newfoundland" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: Elevatorrailfan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Newfoundland_(1862%E2%80%931870).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1610 CE – 1907 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>St. John's</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Guy, Thomas Cochrane, Philip Francis Little</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism, Catholicism, Methodism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Newfoundland Colony</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1758&amp;focus=colony-of-newfoundland" aria-label="Colony of Newfoundland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3449 510 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Newfoundland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3769 766L3220 825M3769 766L4970 663M3769 766L4997 651M3769 766L4997 651M3769 766L3769 766"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3220 825h0M4970 663h0M4997 651h0M4997 651h0M3769 766h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3769 766h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3769 766h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks St. John's. <a href="/atlas?year=1758&amp;focus=colony-of-newfoundland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
